# Curriculum Overview

## What is AI Generated Design all about?
 
#### In **AI Generated Design**, students learn that creating effective digital experiences begins with empathy for the user. Acting as professional UX and UI designers, they plan and build a multi-page web app for a fictional brand, using AI as a creative and technical partner throughout the process. 

#### This is the first unit in the six unit AI Foundations semester 2 course. This professional learning module prepares you to teach it!


## Student Learning Goals
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0; font-weight: bold;">By the end of this unit, students will be able to :</h4>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li>Define a user’s problem and translate it into a purposeful web app plan using personas, sitemaps, and wireframes.
</li> <br>
      <li>Apply computational thinking to structure their designs</li><br>
      <li>Explain and apply core web concepts:<b> HTML</b> for structure and <b>CSS</b>for styling, accessibility, and responsive layouts.</li><br>
      <li>Evaluate AI-generated designs for clarity, usability, and adherence to human-centered design principles.
</li>
    </ul>
